  "query_preview": "..\n(Saturday Night through Wednesday)\nIssued at 852 PM CDT Wed Sep 2 2026\n\nThe upper-ridge looks as if it may temporarily shift back to the \nwest early next week. However, this comes with a word of caution. \nAt least moderate (Level 2/4) heat impacts will continue through \nthe middle of next week as highs in the low to mid 90s are still \nforecast each day. The main difference will be dewpoints which \nwill be modified in wake of a shortwave passage Saturday night, \ndropping the from the mid 70s into the upper 60s. This will keep \nour peak heat index values around 100 degrees each day as opposed \nto 105-110. With ridging still the dominant feature over \ncentral/southern portions of the CONUS, an overall dry forecast \nwill still remain intact. However, with the Tennessee Valley being\non the edge of the ridge, low chances (20%) of diurnally driven \nshowers and thunderstorms will exist each afternoon Sunday through\nWednesday.",
